    "last_assistant_text": "All submissions are successful with `candidate_crashed: true` and `trace_valid: true`.\n\nThe PoC `<break strength=\"invalid\"/>` (30 bytes) triggers a buffer-overflow read in `ProcessSsmlTag` at `ssml.c:866` where `break_value[value]` is accessed with `value = -1` (returned by `attrlookup` for an unrecognized strength attribute). The fix (commit `04ce9728`) adds `if (value < 0) value = 2;` to clamp invalid values.\n\nThree successful submissions were recorded:\n- `poc_break.txt` — `<break strength=\"invalid\"/>` triggers global-buffer-overflow at ssml.c:866\n- `poc_eof.txt` — same tag without closing `>` triggers same crash\n- `poc_eof2.txt` — `hello<b` triggers heap-buffer-overflow at encoding.c:539 (missing EOF check at readclause.c:610)",
